course: dictionary
lesson: 13568
title: Right word, right place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inappropriate means not suitable or not right for a particular time, place or person. To work it out, ask yourself: is this right here, now, for this person? «Shouting during the assembly was inappropriate.» An assembly is a time to listen quietly, so shouting does not fit there.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Her pyjamas were inappropriate for the wedding.» The clue is wedding: a wedding is a smart, special occasion, so pyjamas do not suit it. Try your meaning in the sentence: not suitable for a wedding. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Some inappropriate things are not safe for children. Words, pictures, messages or touching can be inappropriate for a child. If you see or get something that feels wrong, say no, and tell a trusted adult straight away. That is always the right thing to do, and it is never your fault.
fact: Inappropriate means not suitable or not right for a particular time, place or person.
fact: Inappropriately is the adverb: «She spoke inappropriately in class» means she spoke in a way that was not suitable for the classroom.
fact: Phrases you may meet are inappropriate behaviour, inappropriate language and inappropriate for children.
fact: In school, inappropriate behaviour breaks class rules, such as using rude words or shouting in assembly.
fact: For your safety, if anyone shows or sends you something inappropriate, or touches you in a way that feels wrong, say no and tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «Shouting during the assembly was inappropriate.» What does inappropriate mean here? | Exactly what the teacher wanted | Very loud and fun | *Not suitable for that place and time | Quick and tidy
exercise: «Wearing a swimming costume to the library would be inappropriate.» Why? | Costumes are always allowed everywhere | The library has a swimming pool | Libraries are very cold places | *It is not suitable for a library
exercise: Someone sends you a message with pictures that are wrong for a child. What should you do? | Reply with a funny picture back | Keep it secret from everyone, even adults | Forward it to all your friends | *Say no, and tell a trusted adult
test: Ayla says, «Inappropriate language is not allowed in our class.» What does inappropriate language mean? | Words that are very long | Words written in a different language | Words that rhyme | *Words that are not suitable for school
test: Which word means not suitable for a particular time or place? | Careful | *Inappropriate | Polite | Appropriate
exam: Which sentence uses inappropriate correctly? | *«Wearing a party hat to a funeral would be inappropriate.» | «The inappropriate sun came out and warmed the park.» | «Inappropriate is a kind of bread you can toast.» | «She ran inappropriate across the field.»
